","distance":0.7827,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Zac Robinson"},{"season":2024,"team":"DAL","distance":0.7861,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Mike McCarthy"},{"season":2022,"team":"NE","distance":0.8217,"shared":12,"play_caller":null}],"defense":[{"season":2023,"team":"MIA","distance":0.1458,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Vic Fangio"},{"season":2023,"team":"PHI","distance":0.282,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"JAX","distance":0.2838,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Anthony Campanile"},{"season":2023,"team":"SF","distance":0.2948,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"PHI","distance":0.3085,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Jonathan Gannon"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Browns are 6-4 through week 11 of the 2026 season and have been outscored 220 to 188. The defense has done most of the work, ranking 14th in EPA allowed while the offense sits 24th in EPA per play. Their most distinctive trait is the 2nd lowest under center rate in the league.","offense":"The Browns offense has been well below average by EPA per play so far. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Their biggest outliers in how they line up are the 2nd lowest under center rate and the 2nd highest shotgun rate in the league. Deshaun Watson has run the passing game, with KC Concepcion leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Browns defense has been a little above average by EPA allowed per play so far. It has been much better against the pass than the run, ranking 10th and 20th. Maliek Collins has been as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise is Isaiah McGuire, who has 4 sacks, after doing little as a pass rusher a year ago. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is a number of defenders in the box that ranks 8th lowest in the league.","special":"The Browns have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 88% of field goals, which is about average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into the quarterback, about 21% of the money on the books. Their receivers were among the youngest in the league.","players":"Deshaun Watson has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 2,118 yards. Targets have been spread around, with KC Concepcion and Harold Fannin Jr. leading a group where nobody has more than a fifth of the looks. Quinshon Judkins has handled most of the work in the backfield with 68% of the carries. On defense, Isaiah McGuire leads the team with 4 sacks and Denzel Ward has picked off 3 passes.","coaching":"Todd Monken is calling the offense as head coach and Mike Rutenberg is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2023 and 2022 Jaguars. Their defense looks most like the 2023 Dolphins under Vic Fangio and the 2023 Eagles.","trends":"The offense went from 31st in EPA per play in 2025 to 24th so far this season, a modest improvement. The defense moved from 5th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 14th so far this season, a big step back. The biggest change in approach was number of defenders in the box, which went from 6.42 to 6.3.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}